t(25, 1075, """The platforms that talk about the End Times and explain its issues (not the dream channels), those platforms think the events are 3 years, 5 and 10 years away! Many people come to me and say: So-and-so said in 3 years, so-and-so said in 5 years, so-and-so said in 10 years, and one of them said in 50 years!

The comment in brief: all of these, by Allah the Exalted's leave, will be thunderstruck and taken by surprise, because the event will happen while they think it far off""")

t(25, 1475, """Jerusalem .. the moment of the descent of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him .. What I saw I can, by the power of Allah the Exalted, tell of .. But what I have not yet seen is deferred under the will of Allah the Exalted .. The scene of the descent of Allah's prophet Isa I have not yet witnessed until now .. The scene of his killing of the Dajjal I saw, and the confrontation with the Dajjal's army I did not see in all its details; I only saw a bullet that hit me ..
Jerusalem .. the city .. It was not houses of old stone or alleys from the alleys of bygone centuries .. It was a city entirely of modern building like our day today .. In it was the model of modern life, but when our master Isa, peace be upon him, descended there was an intense quiet in it .. As if it were empty and deserted, with no human being in its centre or its outskirts .. As if its houses in its centre and outskirts were all deserted .. its streets empty .. Not a knock on a nail is heard in it .. nor a car moving .. nor shops selling .. An intense stillness and a life absent from the scene of the city .. And around Allah's prophet Isa and those with him, all of us were near Al-Aqsa Mosque, and there were no walls there, and around Al-Aqsa Mosque were modern villas that do not resemble the houses of the alleys of old Jerusalem that exist today! And in the villas many women gather, cooking together with one another, all of them cooking for all the men outside, as if life had turned into communal cooking and communal eating .. Perhaps this is a symbol of the fewness of people, and I do not see it as the mark of people's life after that, for naturally after that every husband, his wife and their children will be in their own home; but my seeing many women gathered, all cooking together, is also not symbolic .. It is a reality .. the reality of the widows who have lost their husbands, and their gathering is because they have no families; they are the ones who lost husbands, sons, brothers and relatives .. To the point that they stop strange men and ask them for help in the affairs of life and its hardships that fall on a woman in a new reality in which there is most likely .. most likely .. no electricity .. Because Jerusalem was silent .. a silent, mute city with no electricity in it .. no cars moving .. no life that ever resembles our life today, and this in turn, and Allah knows best, will create challenges for the women who will live without a husband, children, brothers, fathers or relatives, and they will need strange men to carry out some of life's responsibilities that are hard for a woman.

Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, as I saw, and Allah knows best, will be in a world that to some extent resembles the world he lived in before, apart from the existence of the modern cities that were built during the 2000 years while he was in heaven; so his life after his descent, peace be upon him, will not be identical to his first life before he was raised up, for there will be villas, palaces, bridges, paved roads and empty shopping malls, and a modern life that has stopped .. This is how I saw the features of modern life in the vision .. stopped, with a very intense quiet settled over everything .. As if you were not in a city .. As if you were on an isolated mountain with nothing with you but very intense quiet and stillness .. No existence at all of the life of noise, gatherings and human numbers .. No schools .. no universities .. no many families strolling on the feast days and filling the hills .. Rather, the last of this Ummah are small numbers living the final hours of the life of this world; then the term of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, ends, and most likely, and Allah knows best, he is buried in the Noble Chamber in Madinah. Some will say: how will they get him, peace be upon him, to Madinah .. I say that all of us must begin to prepare ourselves and our minds for things to come that have nothing to do with physics and nothing to do with causes, near or far .. And we must begin to prepare ourselves to understand that the coming stage, from the beginning of the era of the Mahdi, peace be upon him, until the period of the era of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, is two stages in which there will be much through which causes are broken .. So the transport of something in a time with no car, no plane and no train, as is, and Allah knows best, the time of Allah's prophet""")

t(26, 165, """Isa, peace be upon him, is not a matter that should be found very strange if people understand the nature of what is coming correctly.""")

t(26, 395, """On that day wealth will go out to the great cities of the Islamic world only from Jerusalem, by the leave of the Lord, sanctified be every name that is His""")

t(26, 1540, """By the power of Allah our Lord, the Great, the Able, if Allah our Lord, the Great, the Able, wills, and if He intends, decrees, bestows and favours, the poorest of the Muslims will be brought from the east of the earth to its west and from its north to its south, and by the power of Allah they will have a share here in this new world .. So there will be no difference between those in the severest poverty and those who lived in comfort; they will be equal in what is given, in house, in clothing and in food.""")

t(27, 240, """The real Palestine .. not artificial intelligence images .. Some of the brothers, through the artificial intelligence images I publish, may not know that the nature in Palestine is originally like this; so when artificial intelligence draws houses on top of the hills, as in the images I publish, it is something natural and realistic and not from imagination, by the power of our Great Lord""")

t(27, 1445, """A noble brother, dear to my heart, well-mannered and respectable, one of our brothers and loved ones in Alexandria, said to me one day: I made a supplication for you; Allah willing it will be answered. I asked him what it was, and he said: I remembered your vision of years ago, when you said that on the day the Dajjal is killed a bullet came to you from one of the soldiers of the Dajjal's army and you were martyred before Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, so I wished for you to live with our master Isa and witness his time. I said to him: may Allah forgive you, did you dislike martyrdom for your brother (I said it to him jokingly) .. O noble ones

Whoever does not love the time of Allah's prophet Isa, or loves his time: the matter is one of destiny, because we do not choose the time we live in or our life. Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, is a beautiful breath of air and a spirit the like of which can only be seen in our Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, for I have seen none but those two in dreams, upon them be blessings and peace. And this post is because I was asked about the time of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him: what is it like?

It is a very beautiful time in terms of quiet, stillness and the absence of the anxiety that will afflict people for a year, a month and a week because of the Dajjal. It is a very beautiful time, so much so that the earth will give its blessing, as came in the Musnad of Imam Ahmad.

The time of Allah's prophet Isa is a time purely for worship and for turning away completely from this world, because most people will have passed on to the Hereafter and a very small number of people will remain compared with today's numbers, and this is a matter that will sadden those present who remain, over the loss of family and loved ones; but as I said, we do not choose whether we live or do not live, for living is my destiny from Allah the Exalted. So is my joy at departing, in the vision, on that day of the Dajjal's killing, a dislike of the time of Allah's prophet Isa?

Allah forbid; but I am a Muslim, and attaining martyrdom is for any Muslim something that makes any Muslim happy, and this is the last war, with no war after it, so it is the last chance for martyrdom in the path of Allah; and the Dajjal's army is the last army the Muslims will fight, and after that there is no war between the Muslims and any of the nations; war will lay down its burdens completely. So it is a last chance.

Secondly: merely being with our master Isa, peace be upon him, is a beautiful thing and a blessing, and a sharing of life with a human being whose beautiful spirit is too beautiful to be described. It is very hard to describe the beauty of his heart, peace be upon him, like the beauty of the heart of our Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace. And the women will be far more than the men, and the guardian over fifty women is one man who looks after their affairs and does not marry them. And I do not think that electricity will exist, though I am not certain, and this means the difficulty and hardship of life; and perhaps a person like me, and many men and women like you, have tired much in this life, so perhaps we no longer have the effort and energy to live in a life that may need effort to fetch water or to do things that today, in the time of electricity, we do easily. But Allah forbid that there be in the matter any dislike of the time of Allah's prophet Isa; and the fact remains that even if we are deprived of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him, in this world, we are Muslims who know that there is a Hereafter in which we will be gathered, Allah the Exalted willing, and we will see our master Isa, peace be upon him, too.""")

t(28, 160, """So this is a presentation for those who asked to understand the stage of Allah's prophet Isa, peace be upon him. Whoever wants more information, let him post his question, and Allah the Exalted willing I will answer any questions in a new post.""")

t(28, 490, """Yesterday a mountain in Algeria: suddenly water comes out of it like an unceasing waterfall! This news explains to us the reality of the springs and waters that will gush forth, by the leave of Allah the Exalted, from barren and dry places. So, O Muslims: trust in Allah the Exalted and leave despair .. The more you trust in Allah the Exalted, the more He gives you.""")

t(28, 1650, """Some of the new brothers and sisters who follow are asking in some comments: what is the evidence that all this new world will come about? The answer is that what is authentically traced to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, explains all this .. What is authentically traced to him, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, is that the Ummah will become great, and wealth will overflow, not merely increase; and when wealth overflows at a time when all the remaining nations of the earth will be poor and in a great crisis, then all these images are considered a drop from a flood .. When we read the words of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, about the future, we must do one thing after believing and submitting: let our imagination run free while being sure that we are not deluded, because our Prophet, may Allah bless him and his family and grant him peace, spoke truth and revelation; so whoever thinks this is not true, Satan has deceived him and deprived him of the joy.""")

t(29, 2545, """How many children are in the neighbourhood? Their Eid gift is gold pieces""")

t(30, 1180, """In the year 1897 Herzl sat in the city of Basel in Switzerland preparing for the First Zionist Congress, his head filled with almost these very images that I draw and publish .. Herzl dreamed, and his dream came true .. As for us .. it is not a dream .. It is the correction of Herzl's dream .. our cause that we have all carried since we were born .. the re-correction of the world's course .. the world whose threads Herzl wove and then disappeared .. Who among us will be a cause of weaving the threads of the dawn of a new world and then disappear .. The right place for all of you .. all of you .. is here, where these images are .. And one of us will pass through those neighbourhoods with his companions or alone, greeting the inhabitants of the new land .. having a glass of tea or a cup of coffee here and there .. to be assured of the correction of Herzl's dream, because Herzl died and left us his dream .. We may not know who he is today, but if we have life, by the power of our Lord we will know him and see him!""")

t(30, 2525, """Because our children are not less than the children of other nations""")

t(31, 1160, """Today is today .. but today is not ours .. Today is not something we take pride in .. but tomorrow, by Allah's leave, is ours .. Weeping over today will not change the reality of today .. Weeping over today is futility and empty talk. Tomorrow is what matters, by Allah's leave""")

